<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mai Thúc Loan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">died 722</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Mai Hắc Đế, Black Emperor</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mai Thúc Loan was the leader of a large uprising in 722 against Tang Chinese rule in Annan, in what is now northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Proclaiming himself emperor, known as the Black Emperor, he gathered a large army and allied with neighbouring peoples, but a Tang army crushed the revolt. He is honoured in Vietnam as a national hero.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mai-thuc-loan.jpg" alt="Mai Thúc Loan" width="320" height="226" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bảo bảo 123456789 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mai_h%E1%BA%AFc_%C4%91%E1%BA%BF.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
